		(property "Description" "TO-247 heatsink INSULATOR, basic HV-PE (IC-07, D-032): AlN ceramic (aluminium nitride), 1.0 mm, size tab 15.9 x 20.9 mm + 2 x overhang, overhang >= 6.5 mm (creepage 5.0 mm (PD2) and clearance 7.1 mm at 4000 m (insulation report row 'Basic HV-PE, switch node'): 6.5 mm surface + 1.0 mm thickness >= 7.1 mm); Rth c-s 0.20 K/W (AlN 170 W/mK x 1.0 mm, two grease bond lines 50 um at 2.5 W/mK over 15.5 x 20 mm, + 0.05 K/W contact allowance; k values are handbook values (no pad datasheet on file) - confirm with the supplier's data and a thermal test). MOUNTING: spring clip on the plastic body (no screw through the tab hole: a PE screw would need its own insulating bushing and creepage), clip force per the device maker (TO-247: ~50-80 N, ASSUMED). TESTS: type test on the assembled heatsink: AC 2200 V rms 1 min, impulse 6 kV, PD extinction >= 1528 Vpk with <= 10 pC at 1910 Vpk (insulation report); at the claimed altitude's pressure for the PD test"
